Subject: [PATCH 12/22] [M156] [CSD] Guard visual extractor across
 CapturePaintPreview()

Original change's description:
> [CSD] Guard visual extractor across CapturePaintPreview()
>
> **Background**
> PhishingVisualFeatureExtractor::ExtractFeatures() calls
> CapturePaintPreview(), which runs a Blink lifecycle update that can
> synchronously dispatch DOM events. This can ultimately lead to
> CancelPendingImageEmbedding() deleting PhishingVisualFeatureExtractor
> while ExtractFeatures() is still on the stack.
>
> **The Fix**
> Snapshot a WeakPtr before CapturePaintPreview() and return
> early if `this` was destroyed, preventing post-capture member
> reads/writes and callback dispatch on freed memory.
>
> **Testing**
> Add a virtual CapturePaintPreview() test seam and regression
> browser tests covering re-entrant destruction on both capture failure
> and capture success paths.
>
> Test: browser_tests --gtest_filter="PhishingClassifierTest.*" (Default + ASan)
